+Computes the radiance emitted or reflected by a planetary body's surface (ground or water) as seen by an observer, accounting for direct illumination, ambient scattering, and subsurface effects, before applying atmospheric attenuation. It distinguishes itself from pure atmospheric scattering by handling the distinct bidirectional reflectance distribution functions (BRDF) of diffuse terrain and specular water, while integrating precomputed spectral scattering data. [Planetary Surface Shading](9401-planetary-surface-shading.md)
